{"ts": "2026-11-11T06:18:05.008157Z", "run_id": "r-20261111T0604Z-ccb1", "unit": "openspec:add-tool-invocation", "seq": 34, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-004", "id": "Q-004", "status": "answered", "reason": "The frozen test asserts seen deep-equals [\"/found\"] after iterating three rows against a node:http server that pushes req.url on every request. Rows C5 and C6 expect stage response, reason not_json, which the spec defines as a 2xx body that is not JSON or not an object; the only source of 2xx for those routes is the local upstream, so /text and /array must appear. The fake proxy forwards the path unchanged and returns the upstream status, and the gateway client uses redirect manual, so /elsewhere is never requested; the test-plan's [\"/found\"] is C4's own row result. No implementation can satisfy line 275 as written, and the clarifier suggestion is the minimal, spec-consistent correction. Not a fix task; technical kind; the suggestion names the frozen file.", "called": true, "tasks": ["3.3"], "target": null, "kind": "technical", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.4819044999999997, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "bca97f4e059cb7d253560f746290387f4d5404e4910dd90987f1f7c211d2fa36", "checked": [{"ref": "src/runtimes/invoke/invoke.db.test.ts:275", "quote": "assert.deepEqual(r.local.seen, [\"/found\"]);", "claim": "The frozen test asserts the upstream saw only /found after the loop over rows C4 to C6."}, {"ref": "src/runtimes/invoke/invoke.db.test.ts:266", "quote": "for (const [tool, details] of rows) {", "claim": "The assertion at line 275 follows a loop that runs all three rows C4, C5 and C6 before it."}, {"ref": "src/runtimes/invoke/invoke.db.test.ts:96", "quote": "seen.push(req.url ?? \"\");", "claim": "The local upstream records the url of every request it receives, so /text and /array are logged when C5 and C6 reach it."}, {"ref": "src/runtimes/invoke/invoke.db.test.ts:100", "quote": "res.writeHead(200, { \"content-type\": \"text/plain\" }).end(\"ok\");", "claim": "The 2xx text/plain body of C5 is produced by the local upstream, so C5 must reach it."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/tool-invocation/spec.md#scenario-a-call-through-the-fakes-and-each-failure", "quote": "C2 to C8 throw the `details` of their rows (C4 with one request at the local upstream)", "claim": "The spec ties the single-request expectation to row C4 alone, not to the whole run of C4 to C6."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/tool-invocation/spec.md#requirement-invoke-sends-only-what-was-authorised", "quote": "`{ stage: \"response\", reason: \"not_json\" }` for a 2xx body that is not JSON or not an object", "claim": "C5 and C6's not_json result requires a 2xx response, which only the local upstream can give for /text and /array."}, {"ref": "spec:test-plan-runs.md", "quote": "the local upstream saw `[\"/found\"]`", "claim": "The test plan states the [\"/found\"] log as the result column of row C4 only."}, {"ref": "test/support/fake-egress/proxy.ts:250", "quote": "path: q < 0 ? rest : `${rest}?${query}`,", "claim": "The fake proxy forwards the request path unchanged to the upstream, so the upstream sees /found, /text and /array."}, {"ref": "test/support/fake-egress/proxy.ts:268", "quote": "const status = upRes.statusCode ?? 502;", "claim": "The fake proxy passes the upstream's status, including the 302, back to the gateway rather than following it."}, {"ref": "src/gateway/client.ts:319", "quote": "redirect: \"manual\",", "claim": "The gateway client does not follow redirects, so /elsewhere is never requested and the only extra entries are /text and /array."}, {"ref": "src/runtimes/invoke/path.ts:180", "quote": "invoke(): Promise<never> {", "claim": "invoke is still a not-implemented stub at head, so task 3.3 is the one that must satisfy this test and the corrected assertion is reachable."}]}
